 # M4 fixture · legacy peer lower bound
 
-A dsh plugin declaring `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent: ^0.1.0-rc.8` in peer and dev
-dependencies. Under npm semver's prerelease rule this range does **not** match
-`0.1.2-alpha.2`, so installing into an alpha.2 profile emits "Issues with peer
-dependencies" warnings regardless of actual host compatibility (rollup R-08 #3).
-The README claim "the range guarantees host compatibility" is wrong. **Test
-material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
+A dsh **bundle** plugin, `@demo/dsh-peer-bench`, for hosts on the `0.1.x` line.
+It ships three things:
+
+- `cordis.patch.yml` — the `dsh.bundle.patch` layer. It inserts the `peer-bench`
+  row into a profile; the row's module is this package's `index.js`.
+- a declared host range on `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent`, mirrored in
+  `peerDependencies` and `devDependencies`.
+- `apply()` — logs `[peer-bench] apply() executed` through `ctx.effect()` when
+  the row mounts.
+
+## Why the declared range is a union
+
+npm excludes a prerelease version from a range unless the range carries a
+prerelease comparator on the same `[major, minor, patch]` tuple (semver's
+`includePrerelease` option is off by default). The legacy single range
+`^0.1.0-rc.8` therefore admits `0.1.0-rc.8` but **not** the newer
+`0.1.2-alpha.2` host, even though `0.1.2-alpha.2` is the higher version; npm
+reports `ERESOLVE` on a tarball install of the plugin.
+
+Each supported prerelease line needs its own segment. The declared range is now
+the union of the two lines this package supports:
+
+| Declared range | 0.1.0-rc.8 host | 0.1.2-alpha.2 host |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `^0.1.0-rc.8` | admits | **refuses** (npm ERESOLVE) |
+| `^0.1.0-rc.8 \|\| ^0.1.2-alpha.2` | admits | admits |
+
+No static range admits an arbitrary future prerelease tuple: under npm's
+prerelease rule a `0.1.5-rc.1` host is not admitted by either range above,
+because the comparator set has no prerelease at `0.1.5`; each supported line
+needs its own segment. The profile-load check in
+`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/dsh-plugin-compatibility-gate/report.md` covers the
+tracks npm does not: it reads prereleases permissively (like the harness gate
+that shipped later) and refuses a declared floor above the running host, which
+is what pnpm and `link:` installs otherwise accept in silence.
+
+pnpm (the installer `dsh plugin` forwards to) and `link:` installs do not
+reject the legacy range, so the defect only appears on the published-tarball
+npm path. Do not treat the pnpm path as host compatibility.
+
+**Test material only — do not execute or publish** (`"private": true`).
